    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-19139",
      "knowledge_point_id": "91691448-c59a-56dc-a775-d4e9c3297036",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Components",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨3,2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨3,4,1⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{26}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
